# vAIne backend configuration (publishable values only — never secrets).
# Copy to .env for local development; set the same variables in the EAS
# beta environment for TestFlight builds. Values live in the Supabase
# dashboard: vaine-beta -> Project Settings -> API Keys.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY must be the modern publishable key
# (it starts with `sb_publishable_`). The app refuses anything else:
# secret keys (`sb_secret_`), legacy JWT-format keys, service-role keys,
# and pasted private-key material are all rejected at startup. Never put a
# service-role key, secret key, or Apple .p8 key anywhere in the app or
# this repository, and never commit the real values of these variables.
#
# With these unset, the app runs fully local: mock auth, synthetic
# analysis, no network calls.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
